\ User-declarable trait bounds (P7.S3e). A trait lists required member
\ signatures, one type variable per trait; `impl:` gives a type its own
\ member bodies, each inheriting its signature from the trait. A poly word
\ can then require a bound (`'T: Order`)
\ instead of hardcoding one type, and each required member dispatches to the
\ caller's own `impl:` at monomorphization -- an ordinary word call resolved
\ per instantiation, never a runtime vtable.
\
\ `Order` here is by *reference* (`cmp ( &'T &'T -- Rank )`), deliberately
\ distinct from `core::cmp`'s by-value `Ord` (P7.S3s): this file's own point
\ is the `impl:` body-form and a borrowed trait member, not comparison
\ itself, so `Rank`'s three variants are named apart from `core::cmp`'s
\ `Ordering`/`Less`/`Equal`/`Greater` rather than reusing them -- two modules
\ each declaring an enum variant of the same bare name are not otherwise
\ distinguished at a call site inside either one.
import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude | if Bool lt gt | ;

type: Rank
| Under
| Same
| Over
;

trait: Order 'T
  cmp ( &'T &'T -- Rank )
;

trait: Show 'T
  show ( &'T -- )
;

type: Point x i64 y i64 ;

\ Satisfaction is nominal, not structural: an `impl:` block declares a
\ type's own concrete words as trait members, inheriting each member's
\ signature from the trait with the trait's `'T` substituted for the
\ concrete type.
impl: Order for Point
  : cmp
    | a b |
    a &y @ | ay |
    b &y @ | by |
    ay by lt
    ~[ Under ]
    ~[
      ay by gt
      ~[ Over ]
      ~[
        a &x @ | ax |
        b &x @ | bx |
        ax bx lt
        ~[ Under ]
        ~[
          ax bx gt
          ~[ Over ] ~[ Same ] if
        ] if
      ] if
    ] if ;
;

impl: Show for Point
  : show
    | p | "(" . p &x @ . "," . p &y @ . ")" . ;
;

\ Bounds compose: `'T: Order Show` is the existing `'T: Copy Ord`-style
\ capability list, greedy over N names. `cmp`/`show` dispatch as ordinary
\ required members, resolved against the caller's own `impl:` at
\ monomorphization -- an ordinary word call, never a quotation value or a
\ runtime vtable.
: show_larger ( &'T: Order Show &'T -- )
  | b | | a |
  a b cmp
  ~[ ( Under ) drop b show ]
  ~[ ( Same )  drop a show ]
  ~[ ( Over )  drop a show ]
  Rank? ;

: main ( -- )
  0 0 Point | origin |
  3 4 Point | corner |
  &origin &corner show_larger
  origin drop
  corner drop ;
